{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to a Matomo installation as events, through its bulk tracking API."}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sending-to-Matomo","title":"Sending to Matomo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/matomo(url:siteID:dimensions:category:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/matomo(url:siteID:dimensions:category:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoSetupError"]},{"anchor":"Custom-dimensions","title":"Custom dimensions","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoDimensions","doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoUnmappedProperty"]},{"anchor":"Encoding-batches","title":"Encoding batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoBatchEncoder"]},{"anchor":"Records-left-out","title":"Records left out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoEncodingError"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/matomo(url:siteID:dimensions:category:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"makes an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","type":"reference"},{"text":") for one site of a Matomo installation in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one call. It checks the installation’s URL, the site ID, the category and the custom dimensions,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"then posts bulk tracking requests to the installation’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"matomo.php","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoBatchEncoder","type":"reference"},{"text":". Each batch is split to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","type":"reference"},{"text":": 20 records a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request, as Matomo’s iOS SDK sends them, and 1,000,000 bytes a request, under the 1 MiB that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nginx takes in a body by default, as Matomo documents no limit. A batch with no record the encoder","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can write, an empty one included, makes no request. The destination retries no response, a 5xx,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"408 and 429, and drops and reports any other status. No trace context is sent. ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"leaves this module out, so import it on its own.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Matomo takes events from anyone who can reach it, so the destination needs no key, and builds on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every platform: an app sends to Matomo directly."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import MatomoEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let matomo = try HTTPDestination.matomo(","    url: url,  \/\/ where Matomo is installed: https:\/\/analytics.example.com","    siteID: 3,  \/\/ the app's site in Matomo","    dimensions: [\"plan\": 1],  \/\/ custom dimensions made in Matomo","    category: \"Shop\",  \/\/ each event's category","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: matomo)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"url","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is where Matomo is installed, with its path if it has one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"https:\/\/example.com\/matomo\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), not the tracker’s endpoint: the destination appends ","type":"text"},{"code":"matomo.php","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"itself. The factory throws ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoSetupError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for a URL that isn’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"https","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", has no host, holds a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"user name, password, query or fragment, or already ends in a ","type":"text"},{"code":".php","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" file such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"matomo.php","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a site ID below 1; for a category that is empty once trimmed, or longer than the 4,096 characters","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Matomo stores; and for dimensions that break a rule, listed below.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"No token_auth","anchor":"No-tokenauth"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The destination sends no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"token_auth"},{"type":"text","text":", and takes none. A token is a secret, and anything an app"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ships can be read out of it, so a token in an app gives anyone who has the app the token’s rights"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"over your Matomo."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Without a token, Matomo takes an event’s time (","type":"text"},{"code":"cdt","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") only when it is less than a day old, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"refuses one more than a day ahead. It answers 200 to such a request all the same, and stores","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing, so the encoder leaves out every record tracked more than 23 hours before or after it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encodes the batch, and the destination reports it, the hour to spare for a queue on the server and clocks that disagree. So a record that waits","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"more than 23 hours to be encoded, kept by a store through a long time offline or waiting in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"buffer behind a failing delivery, is reported as ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoEncodingError\/timestampOutsideWindow","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and never reaches Matomo.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A request is encoded once, and each retry sends the same bytes, so the encoder gives each request"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a deadline 23 hours after its oldest record was tracked. A request still failing by then isn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent again, as it would reach Matomo too late to be stored: the destination drops the whole"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"request, its younger records too, and reports it on "},{"code":"dropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.deadlineExceeded(deadline:recordIDs:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", with every one of its records’ identifiers. Only the past side of the window needs a deadline: a retry arrives later, never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"earlier, so it can’t carry a record further ahead of Matomo’s clock than it was. The window is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measured with the device’s clock, which Matomo can’t see: a device whose clock is wrong by more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than a day has every record refused, without an error. A clock that reads NaN or infinite has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every record left out and reported."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To keep older records, send them to a server you run, such as a TraffluentCollector, and have"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that server forward them to Matomo with a token of a user who has write access to the site,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"added as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"token_auth"},{"type":"text","text":" to its bulk request’s JSON. A token on a server stays secret. This module"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doesn’t do that."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Visitors are sessions","anchor":"Visitors-are-sessions"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Matomo counts a visitor per "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_id"},{"type":"text","text":", 16 hexadecimal digits. The destination sends the last 64 bits"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the record’s session, from the sessions enricher, in lowercase hex. Nothing else identifies a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record: no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uid"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cid"},{"type":"text","text":", device identifier or account. So Matomo’s visitors are sessions, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its returning-visitor and visits-per-visitor reports say how long sessions last, not whether"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"people come back. That is the library’s default, for privacy. Each session is one visit as long"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as the sessions enricher’s timeout is no longer than Matomo’s visit length, 30 minutes by default"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"visit_standard_length"},{"type":"text","text":"). With a longer timeout, a session that pauses for longer than Matomo’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"visit length becomes two visits of one visitor."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A record with no session, from a tracker without the sessions enricher, is its own visitor: its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the last 64 bits of the record’s identifier. A record a store recovered after a relaunch","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keeps its session, and with it the ","type":"text"},{"code":"_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of its first send. Making up a session would join unrelated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"records, and skipping the record would lose it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Matomo recognizes a visitor by "},{"code":"_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and, failing that, by a fingerprint of the request’s IP"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"address, User-Agent, language and a daily salt, within 30 minutes. A new session’s first event"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has an "},{"code":"_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" Matomo hasn’t seen, so Matomo may fold it into another visit from the same address"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and User-Agent: an earlier session on the same device, or a session of another person behind the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same network. Set "},{"code":"trust_visitors_cookies = 1","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" under "},{"code":"[Tracker]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in Matomo’s "},{"code":"config.ini.php","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"have Matomo match a request that has an "},{"code":"_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" by its "},{"code":"_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" alone, for every site of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"installation. When Matomo’s privacy setting"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to force tracking without cookies is on, Matomo ignores "},{"code":"_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and every visit is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fingerprint’s."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Matomo records the address each request comes from, as no app can override it without a token.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"It masks part of the address before storing it when “Anonymize Visitors’ IP addresses” is on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(Administration, Privacy, Anonymize data). In Matomo 5.14 and 6.0 it is on, masking 2 bytes, for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an installation whose administrator has never changed it, so a fresh install has it on, and an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"older one keeps the setting it had. Matomo still uses the full address for geolocation and for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the fingerprint above unless “Also use the Anonymized IP addresses when enriching visits” is on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"too, which is off by default. Check both settings before you send.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"What Matomo receives","anchor":"What-Matomo-receives"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each request is a JSON object, "},{"code":"{\"requests\":[…]}","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", holding one tracking request per record, oldest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first: "},{"code":"?","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and a query string, every value percent-encoded but for letters, digits, "},{"code":"-","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":".","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"_","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and "},{"code":"~","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Each tracking request is a Matomo event:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Parameter"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"idsite","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The site ID","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"rec","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"apiv","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_id"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The session’s last 64 bits, or the record’s"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"cdt","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s time, in whole seconds since 1970"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ca"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so Matomo doesn’t take the request for a page view should its Events plugin be off","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"e_c"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The category you give, such as your app’s name","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"e_a"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s name"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"lang","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s locale, as a BCP 47 identifier, when it has "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocaleKey"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dimension<ID>"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The value of each property the dimensions map","type":"text"}]}]]]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Matomo’s Events reports group events by category, then action, then name. The category is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"argument you give, as an app’s events have no grouping Matomo would show better, and the action is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the event’s name, so the Event Actions report lists your events. No event name ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"e_n"},{"type":"text","text":") or value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"e_v"},{"type":"text","text":") is sent."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The User-Agent is the one ","type":"text"},{"code":"URLSession","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sends, which Matomo reads for the device and operating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system. The rest of the standard context isn’t sent.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Custom dimensions","anchor":"Custom-dimensions"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Matomo numbers each site’s custom dimensions as you make them (Administration, Websites, Custom"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Dimensions), so "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoDimensions","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" maps your plan’s property names to their IDs:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[\"plan\": 1, \"seats\": 2]"},{"type":"text","text":". A property is mapped by name in every event that has it. Its value is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"read through the event’s schema in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":": a string as it is, a number as JSON writes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it, a Boolean as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":", and an array or object as its JSON. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" sends no value."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" property is never sent, whatever the record reveals, so it can’t be mapped."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A property no dimension is mapped to is never sent, and the record goes without it. When the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination is made, it logs a notice for each event with such properties, once."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoDimensions\/unmappedProperties(in:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" lists them, so a test can check that every property"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you mean to send has a dimension."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The factory throws for a dimension ID below 1, a property mapped twice, a property no event of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plan has, a property that is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" in an event, and two properties of one event mapped to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one dimension, checked in that order."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make each dimension in Matomo with the Action scope, so each event keeps its own value. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dimension of the Visit scope holds one value a visit, the last one sent. Matomo ignores a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dimension it has no dimension of that ID for, and stores at most 250 characters of a value."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Records left out","anchor":"Records-left-out"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write, or that Matomo would refuse or change, is left out and the rest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the batch is sent:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one the plan doesn’t describe, whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or that holds a value JSON can’t;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose event name is empty once Matomo removes line breaks and trims it, or longer than the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"4,096 characters Matomo stores of an action;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose timestamp has no whole seconds of ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int64","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or is more than 23 hours from when the batch","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is encoded;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one with a dimension’s value longer than 250 characters;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose tracking request is more than a request of 1,000,000 bytes can hold.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Lengths are counted as Matomo stores the text: without line breaks or NUL characters, trimmed of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"spaces and tabs at either end, and with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"&"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":">"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\""},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"'"},{"text":" written as the HTML entities","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Matomo stores them as, so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"&"},{"text":" counts 5. Matomo removes the line breaks and trims the spaces of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"name or value it keeps too.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The destination reports each as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"text":", a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"text":" whose reason is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoEncodingError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". When the destination is made, it logs a notice for each event of the plan","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whose name would be left out.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"What Matomo doesn’t report","anchor":"What-Matomo-doesnt-report"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Matomo answers 200 to a bulk request it can read, whatever its tracking requests hold. One it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"refuses is counted as ","type":"text"},{"code":"invalid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the answer’s JSON and not stored, and only a request with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"token learns which. When the answer says Matomo refused every one, as for a site ID of no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"site, the destination drops the request and reports it as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.rejectedInBody(status:reason:recordIDs:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". When it tracked some and refused","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"others, the refused ones are lost with only a notice in the log, as the answer doesn’t say which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"they were. When its counts add up to fewer than the request’s tracking requests, or are both 0,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Matomo skipped some without saying so, as after a database lock wait timeout, and the destination","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sends the request again until its deadline; Matomo counts the ones it had tracked twice. Whether","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a server with the QueuedTracking plugin counts queued requests as tracked is unverified: if it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"doesn’t, every request there is sent again until its deadline. Check that the first events show","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"up in the site’s Visits Log.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A server set to require a token for every bulk request (","type":"text"},{"code":"bulk_requests_require_authentication","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":")","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"refuses each one: Matomo 6.0 answers 400, which the destination drops and reports, and Matomo 5.14","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"answers 500, which the destination retries until the request is cancelled. Leave that setting","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"off.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Matomo doesn’t remove duplicates. A record is sent more than once when a request is retried after"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Matomo stored it but the answer was lost, when a delivery sends a cancelled batch again, and when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a store redelivers records after a relaunch, and Matomo counts each copy."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what Matomo receives, and why, in more detail.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding"},"metadata":{"role":"collection","externalID":"MatomoEncoding","roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"MatomoEncoding"}],"title":"MatomoEncoding","symbolKind":"module"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/matomoencoding"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"role":"collection","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","abstract":[{"text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","kind":"symbol","title":"HTTPDestinations"},"doc://MatomoEncoding/documentation/MatomoEncoding/MatomoDimensions/unmappedProperties(in:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"The properties of ","type":"text"},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s events that no mapping names, and that Matomo is never sent.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/matomoencoding\/matomodimensions\/unmappedproperties(in:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoDimensions\/unmappedProperties(in:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"unmappedProperties"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"in"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TrackingPlan","preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MatomoUnmappedProperty","preciseIdentifier":"s:14MatomoEncoding0A16UnmappedPropertyV"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"unmappedProperties(in:)","kind":"symbol"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/choosingdestinations":{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","title":"Choosing Destinations","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Choosing Destinations","type":"text"}],"type":"link"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/BatchEncoder":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"What turns a batch of records into the requests ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","type":"reference"},{"text":" sends.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/batchencoder","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"BatchEncoder","kind":"symbol"},"doc://MatomoEncoding/documentation/MatomoEncoding/MatomoEncodingError":{"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MatomoEncodingError"}],"type":"topic","title":"MatomoEncodingError","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/matomoencoding\/matomoencodingerror","identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/docume